# Environment configuration index.
#
# There is intentionally no root-level `.env`: each app reads its own file.
#
#   backend/.env.example   -> copy to backend/.env   (Django; contains secrets)
#   frontend/.env.example  -> copy to frontend/.env  (Vite; public values only)
#
# Real `.env` files are ignored by Git — never commit them. Only `.env.example`
# files are tracked, and they contain placeholders only.
#
# See docs/environments.md for the full environment strategy.

# --- Planned (not yet used; will move to the owning app's .env.example) ---
